You neither see the rocks bristling not far off in the bed of the flood,

62
00:05:07,459 --> 00:05:09,659
nor hear the breakers boil at their base.

63
00:05:10,735 --> 00:05:17,860
But I tell you, and you may mark my words, you will come someday to a craggy pass in

64
00:05:17,861 --> 00:05:20,983
the channel, where the whole of life's stream will

65
00:05:20,984 --> 00:05:25,060
be broken up into whirl and tumult, foam and noise.

66
00:05:25,965 --> 00:05:30,919
Either you will be dashed to atoms on crag points, or lifted up and born on by some

67
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:34,060
master wave into a calmer current, as I am now.

68
00:05:35,375 --> 00:05:36,375
I like this day.

69
00:05:37,119 --> 00:05:38,819
I like that sky of steel.

70
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:42,979
I like the sternness and stillness of the world under this frost.

71
00:05:43,979 --> 00:05:44,979
I like Thornfield.

72
00:05:45,759 --> 00:05:50,419
It's antiquity, it's retirement, it's old crotries and thorn trees,

73
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:55,080
it's gray facade and lines of dark windows reflecting that metal wellkin,

74
00:05:56,209 --> 00:05:59,414
and yet how long have I abhorred the very thought of it,

75
00:05:59,415 --> 00:06:04,040
shunned it like a great plague house, how I do still abhor.

76
00:06:05,389 --> 00:06:09,496
He ground his teeth and was silent, he arrested his

77
00:06:09,546 --> 00:06:13,040
step and struck his boot against the hard ground.

78
00:06:14,419 --> 00:06:18,273
Some hated thought seemed to have him in its grip,

79
00:06:18,274 --> 00:06:21,401
and to hold him so tightly that he could not advance.

80
00:06:23,169 --> 00:06:28,400
We were ascending the avenue when he thus paused, the hall was before us.

81
00:06:29,439 --> 00:06:32,452
Lifting his eye to its battlements, he cast over

82
00:06:32,453 --> 00:06:36,159
them a glare such as I never saw before or since.

83
00:06:37,099 --> 00:06:44,400
Pain, shame, ire, impatience, disgust, detestation seemed momentarily to hold a

84
00:06:44,401 --> 00:06:48,659
quivering conflict in the large pupil dilating under his ebony brow.

85
00:06:49,990 --> 00:06:53,742
Wild was the wrestle, which should be paramount,

86
00:06:53,743 --> 00:06:57,041
but another feeling rose and triumphed.

87
00:06:57,479 --> 00:07:01,360
Something hard and cynical, self-willed and resolute.

88
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:05,200
It settled his passion and petrified his countenance.

89
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:06,900
He went on.

90
00:07:08,250 --> 00:07:10,939
During the moment I was silent, miss air.

91
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:14,040
I was arranging a point with my destiny.

92
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:20,240
She stood there by that beach-trunk, a hag like one of those who appeared to

93
00:07:20,439 --> 00:07:21,919
Macbeth on the heath of forest.

94
00:07:23,619 --> 00:07:24,619
You like Thornfield?

95
00:07:25,389 --> 00:07:31,040
She said, lifting her finger, and then she wrote in the air a memento, which ran in

96
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:33,931
lured, hieroglyphics all along the housefront,

97
00:07:33,932 --> 00:07:36,661
between the upper and lower row of windows.

98
00:07:37,939 --> 00:07:40,779
Like it if you can, like it if you dare.

99
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:46,979
I will like it, said I, I dare like it, and he subjoined moodily.

100
00:07:47,819 --> 00:07:52,080
I will keep my word, I will break obstacles to happiness, to goodness,

101
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:56,880
yes goodness, I wish to be a better man than I have been, than I am.

102
00:07:57,619 --> 00:08:02,599
As Job's Leviathan broke the spear, the dart, and the habition, hindrances,

103
00:08:03,279 --> 00:08:08,400
which others count as iron and brass, I will esteem but straw and rotten wood.

104
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:13,000
Adele here ran before him with her shuttlecock.

105
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:19,240
Away, he cried harshly, keep at a distance child, or go into Sufi.

106
00:08:20,349 --> 00:08:24,576
Continuing then, to pursue his walk in silence, I ventured

107
00:08:24,577 --> 00:08:28,419
to recall him to the point whence he had abruptly diverged.

108
00:08:29,409 --> 00:08:33,900
Did you leave the balcony, sir, I asked, when Mamazelle Varens entered.

109
00:08:35,509 --> 00:08:41,279
I almost expected a rebuff for this hardly well-timed question, but on the contrary,

110
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:46,619
waking out of his scowling abstraction, he turned his eyes towards me.

111
00:08:47,259 --> 00:08:49,259
And the shade seemed to clear off his brow.

112
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,279
Oh, I had forgotten Selene.

113
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:54,479
Well, to resume.

114
00:08:55,479 --> 00:09:00,259
When I saw my charmer thus come in, accompanied by a cavalier, I seemed to

115
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:06,220
hear a hiss and the green snake of jealousy, rising on undulating coils from

116
00:09:06,221 --> 00:09:09,579
the moonlit balcony, glided within my waistcoat,

117
00:09:09,603 --> 00:09:12,959
and ate its way in two minutes to my heart's core.

118
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:19,279
Strange, he exclaimed, suddenly starting again from the point.

119
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:24,479
Strange that I should choose you for the confidant of all this young lady.

120
00:09:25,634 --> 00:09:31,299
Passing strange that you should listen to me quietly, as if it were the most usual

121
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:34,116
thing in the world for a man like me to tell stories of his

122
00:09:34,117 --> 00:09:38,400
opera mistresses to acquaint inexperienced girl like you.

123
00:09:39,549 --> 00:09:44,860
But the last singularity explains the first, as I intimated once before.

124
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:49,540
You, with your gravity, considerateness and

125
00:09:49,541 --> 00:09:53,800
caution, were made to be the recipient of secrets.

126
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:59,380
Besides, I know what sort of a mind I have placed in communication with my own.

127
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,639
I know it is one not liable to take infection.

128
00:10:03,479 --> 00:10:05,020
It is a peculiar mind.

129
00:10:05,599 --> 00:10:06,799
It is a unique one.

130
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:13,001
Happily, I do not mean to harm it, but if I did, it would not take harm from me.

131
00:10:13,479 --> 00:10:17,380
The more you and I converse the better, for while I cannot blight you,

132
00:10:17,939 --> 00:10:18,939
you may refresh me.

133
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,580
After this digression, he proceeded.

134
00:10:23,805 --> 00:10:25,220
I remained in the balcony.

135
00:10:26,799 --> 00:10:32,419
They will come to her boudoir no doubt, thought I, let me prepare an ambush.

136
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:38,020
So putting my hand in through the open window, I drew the curtain over it,

137
00:10:38,599 --> 00:10:41,119
leaving only an opening through which I could take observations.

138
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:46,557
Then I closed the casement, all but a chink, just wide

139
00:10:46,558 --> 00:10:50,279
enough to furnish an outlet to lovers whispered vows.

140
00:10:51,110 --> 00:10:55,819
Then I stole back to my chair, and as I resumed it, the pair came in.

141
00:10:56,919 --> 00:10:58,680
My eye was quickly at the aperture.

142
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:05,540
Selene's chamber-made entered, little lamp, left it on the table, and withdrew.

143
00:11:06,610 --> 00:11:09,526
The couple with us revealed to me clearly, both

144
00:11:09,526 --> 00:11:12,800
removed their cloaks, and there was the variance.

145
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:20,419
Shining in satin and jewels, my gifts of course, and there was her companion in an

146
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:26,759
officer's uniform, and I knew him for a young Rueh of a Vicente, a brainless and

147
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:30,675
vicious youth, whom I had sometimes met in society, and had

148
00:11:30,676 --> 00:11:35,220
never thought of hating because I despised him so absolutely.

149
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:41,360
On recognizing him, the fang of the snake jealousy was instantly broken,

150
00:11:42,130 --> 00:11:47,000
because at the same moment, my love for Selene sank under an extinguisher,

151
00:11:47,869 --> 00:11:52,840
a woman who could betray me for such a rival was not worth contending for.

152
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:59,520
She deserved only scorn, less, however, than I, who had been her dupe.

153
00:12:00,939 --> 00:12:02,020
They began to talk.

154
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:09,080
Their conversation eased me completely, frivolous, mercenary, heartless,

155
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,560
and senseless.

156
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:14,479
It was rather calculated to weary than in rage a listener.

157
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:21,460
A card of mine lay on the table, this being perceived brought my name under discussion.

158
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:27,639
Neither of them possessed energy or wit to belabor me soundly, but they insulted me

159
00:12:27,689 --> 00:12:33,939
as causally as they could in their little way, especially Selene, who even waxed

160
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:39,020
rather brilliant on my personal defects, deformities she termed them.

161
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:45,439
Now it had been her custom to launch out into fervent admiration of what she called

162
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:52,200
my butemail, wherein she differed diametrically from you, who told me point

163
00:12:52,201 --> 00:12:56,319
blank at the second interview, that you did not think me handsome.

164
00:12:57,430 --> 00:13:01,659
The contrast struck me at the time, and Adele here came running up again.

165
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:08,960
Monsieur, John has just been to say that your agent has called and wishes to see you.

166
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:12,000
Ah, in that case I must abridge.

167
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:18,380
Opening the window, I walked in upon them, liberated Selene from my protection,

168
00:13:19,419 --> 00:13:24,340
gave her notice to vacate her hotel, offered her a purse for immediate

169
00:13:24,341 --> 00:13:29,900
exigencies, disregarded screams, hysterics, prayers, protestations,

170
00:13:32,459 --> 00:13:40,459
convulsions, made an appointment with the I had the pleasure of encountering him,

171
00:13:41,319 --> 00:13:47,119
left a bullet in one of his poor etiolated arms, feeble as the wing of a chicken in

172
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:51,020
the pip, and then thought I had done with the whole crew.

173
00:13:52,090 --> 00:13:57,779
But unluckily the varen's six months before had given me this filet Adele,

174
00:13:58,509 --> 00:14:04,500
who she affirmed was my daughter, and perhaps she may be, though I see no

175
00:14:04,501 --> 00:14:07,860
proofs of such grim paternity written in her countenance.

176
00:14:09,299 --> 00:14:11,900
Pilate is more like me than she.

177
00:14:12,970 --> 00:14:16,682
Some years after I had broken with the mother, she abandoned

178
00:14:16,683 --> 00:14:19,759
her child and ran away to Italy with a musician or singer.

179
00:14:21,055 --> 00:14:25,639
I acknowledged no natural claim on Adele's part to be supported

180
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:30,000
by me, nor do I now acknowledge any, for I am not her father.

181
00:14:31,069 --> 00:14:36,720
But hearing that she was quite destitute, Iean took the poor thing out of the slime

182
00:14:36,721 --> 00:14:40,402
and mud of Paris and transplanted it here to grow up

183
00:14:40,403 --> 00:14:43,799
clean in the wholesome soil of an English country garden.

184
00:14:45,639 --> 00:14:49,819
Mrs Fairfax found you to train it, but now you know that it is the

185
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:52,700
illegitimate offspring of a French opera girl.

186
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:57,479
You will perhaps think differently of your post and protégé.

187
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:03,580
You will be coming to me someday with notice that you have found another place,

188
00:15:04,549 --> 00:15:07,639
that you beg me to look out for a new governess, etc.

189
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,240
Eh?

190
00:15:09,599 --> 00:15:10,599
No.

191
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:14,119
Adele is not answerable for either her mother's faults or yours.

192
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,240
I have a regard for her.

193
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:23,759
And now that I know she is, in a sense, parentless, forsaken by her mother and

194
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:28,180
disowned by you, sir, I shall cling closer to her than before.

195
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:34,819
How could I possibly prefer the spoiled pet of a wealthy family who would hate her

196
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:40,721
governess as a nuisance, to a lonely little orphan who leans towards her as a friend?

197
00:15:41,849 --> 00:15:45,099
Oh, that is the light in which you view it.

198
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:49,540
Well, I must go in now, and you too, it darkens.

199
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:56,299
But I stayed out a few minutes longer with Adele and pilot, ran a race with her,

200
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,020
and played a game of battle-door and shuttlecock.

201
00:16:00,869 --> 00:16:06,840
When we went in, and I had removed her bonnet and coat, I took her on my knee,

202
00:16:07,759 --> 00:16:13,419
kept her there an hour, allowing her to prattle as she liked, not rebuking even

203
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:17,819
some little freedoms and trivialities into which she was apt to stray when much

204
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:24,240
noticed, and which betrayed in her a superficiality of character inherited

205
00:16:24,241 --> 00:16:28,500
probably from her mother, hardly congenial to an English mind.

206
00:16:29,299 --> 00:16:32,734
Still, she had her merits, and I was disposed to

207
00:16:32,735 --> 00:16:36,080
appreciate all that was good in her, to the utmost.

208
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:43,400
I sought in her countenance and features a likeness to Mr. Rochester, but found none,

209
00:16:44,119 --> 00:16:48,220
no trait, no turn of expression announced relationship.

210
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,993
It was a pity, if she could but have been proved

211
00:16:53,994 --> 00:16:57,100
to resemble him, he would have thought more of her.

212
00:16:58,599 --> 00:17:03,840
It was not till after I had withdrawn to my own chamber for the night, that I

213
00:17:03,841 --> 00:17:07,659
steadily reviewed the tale Mr. Rochester had told me.

214
00:17:08,779 --> 00:17:12,425
As he had said, there was probably nothing at all

215
00:17:12,426 --> 00:17:16,119
extraordinary in the substance of the narrative itself.

216
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:22,159
A wealthy Englishman's passion for a French dancer and her treachery to him,

217
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:26,919
where every day matters enough, no doubt, in society.

218
00:17:28,549 --> 00:17:33,959
But there was something decidedly strange in the paroxysm of emotion, which had

219
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:38,979
suddenly seized him, when he was in the act of expressing the present contentment

220
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:44,819
of his mood, and his newly revived pleasure in the old hall and its environs.

221
00:17:45,709 --> 00:17:50,116
I meditated wonderingly on this incident, but gradually

222
00:17:50,116 --> 00:17:53,479
quitting it as I found it for the present inexplicable.

223
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:58,180
I turned to the consideration of my master's manner to myself.

224
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:04,820
The confidence he had thought fit to reposing me seemed a tribute to my discretion.

225
00:18:05,409 --> 00:18:08,419
I regarded and accepted it as such.

226
00:18:09,729 --> 00:18:15,520
His deportment had now for some weeks been more uniform towards me than at the first.

227
00:18:16,509 --> 00:18:18,020
I never seemed in his way.

228
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:21,180
He did not take fits of chilling hotur.

229
00:18:22,209 --> 00:18:26,080
When he met me unexpectedly, the encounter seemed welcome.

230
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:30,220
He had always a word and sometimes a smile for me.

231
00:18:30,959 --> 00:18:36,700
When summoned by formal invitation to his presence, I was honoured by a cordiality

232
00:18:36,701 --> 00:18:42,040
of reception that made me feel I really possessed the power to amuse him.

233
00:18:42,939 --> 00:18:45,669
And that these evening conferences were sought

234
00:18:45,669 --> 00:18:49,001
as much for his pleasure as for my benefit.

235
00:18:49,599 --> 00:18:55,779
I indeed talked comparatively little, but I heard him talk with relish.

236
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,540
It was his nature to be communicative.

237
00:18:59,159 --> 00:19:02,068
He liked to open to a mind unequainted with

238
00:19:02,069 --> 00:19:06,041
the world, glimpses of its scenes and ways.

239
00:19:06,099 --> 00:19:11,479
I do not mean its corrupt scenes and wicked ways, but such has derived their

240
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:15,698
interest from the great scale on which they were acted,

241
00:19:15,699 --> 00:19:18,380
the strange novelty by which they were characterized.

242
00:19:19,689 --> 00:19:26,139
And I had a keen delight in receiving the new ideas he offered, in imagining the new

243
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:31,000
pictures he portrayed, and following him in thought through the new regions he

244
00:19:31,001 --> 00:19:36,459
disclosed, never startled or troubled by one noxious illusion.

245
00:19:38,169 --> 00:19:43,299
The ease of his manner freed me from painful restraint, the friendly frankness,

246
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:48,779
as correct as cordial, with which he treated me, drew me to him.

247
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:54,540
I felt at times as if he were my relation rather than my master, yet he was

248
00:19:54,541 --> 00:19:57,939
imperious sometimes still, but I did not mind that.

249
00:19:58,560 --> 00:19:59,560
I saw it was his way.

250
00:20:00,319 --> 00:20:05,400
So happy, so gratified did I become with this new interest added to life,

251
00:20:06,159 --> 00:20:08,259
that I ceased to pine after kindred.

252
00:20:08,939 --> 00:20:11,919
My thin, present destiny seemed to enlarge.

253
00:20:12,569 --> 00:20:14,860
The blanks of existence were filled up.

254
00:20:15,619 --> 00:20:17,020
My bodily health improved.

255
00:20:17,849 --> 00:20:19,700
I gathered flesh and strength.

256
00:20:20,919 --> 00:20:23,520
And was Mr. Rochester now ugly in my eyes?

257
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,240
No, reader.

258
00:20:26,479 --> 00:20:32,180
Gratitude, and many associations, all pleasurable and genial, made his face

259
00:20:32,181 --> 00:20:34,973
the object I best like to see, his presence in a

260
00:20:34,973 --> 00:20:37,779
room was more cheering than the brightest fire.

261
00:20:39,159 --> 00:20:41,040
Yet I had not forgotten his faults.

262
00:20:42,139 --> 00:20:45,680
Indeed, I could not, for he brought them frequently before me.

263
00:20:46,759 --> 00:20:52,580
He was proud, sardonic, harsh, to inferiority of every description.

264
00:20:53,590 --> 00:20:57,858
In my secret soul, I knew that his great kindness to

265
00:20:57,859 --> 00:21:01,200
me was balanced by unjust severity to many others.

266
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,779
He was moody too, unaccountably so.

267
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:11,099
I more than once, when sent for to read to him, found him sitting in his library

268
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:14,880
alone with his head bent on his folded arms.

269
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:23,260
And when he looked up, a morose, almost a malignant scowl blackened his features.

270
00:21:23,459 --> 00:21:27,919
But I believed that his moodyness, his harshness and his former faults of

271
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:32,068
morality, I say, former, for now he seemed corrected

272
00:21:32,069 --> 00:21:36,080
of them, had their source in some cruel cross of fate.

273
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:41,680
I believed he was naturally a man of better tendencies, higher principles,

274
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:45,604
and purer tastes than such as circumstances had

275
00:21:45,605 --> 00:21:50,319
developed, education instilled, or destiny encouraged.

276
00:21:51,590 --> 00:21:54,850
I thought there were excellent materials in him, though for

277
00:21:54,851 --> 00:21:58,240
the present they hung together somewhat spoiled and tangled.

278
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:03,525
I cannot deny that I grieved for his grief, whatever

279
00:22:03,526 --> 00:22:06,939
that was, and would have given much to assuage it.

280
00:22:08,150 --> 00:22:13,279
Though I had now extinguished my candle and was laid down in bed, I could not

281
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:18,759
sleep for thinking of his look when he paused in the avenue, and told how his

282
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:23,919
destiny had risen up before him, and dared him to be happy at Thornfield.

283
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:27,240
Why not, I asked myself?

284
00:22:28,279 --> 00:22:30,180
What alienates him from the house?

285
00:22:30,959 --> 00:22:32,299
Will he leave it again soon?

286
00:22:33,099 --> 00:22:37,159
Mrs. Fairfax said he seldom stayed here longer than a fortnight at a time,

287
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,840
and he has now been resident eight weeks.

288
00:22:41,799 --> 00:22:44,619
If he does go, the change will be doleful.

289
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:48,114
Suppose he should be absent spring, summer and

290
00:22:48,115 --> 00:22:51,779
autumn, how joyless sunshine and fine days will seem.

291
00:22:53,639 --> 00:22:56,599
I hardly know whether I had slept or not after this musing.

292
00:22:57,439 --> 00:23:02,240
At any rate, I started wide awake on hearing a vague murmur, peculiar and

293
00:23:02,241 --> 00:23:05,119
legubrious, which sounded I thought just above me.

294
00:23:06,169 --> 00:23:09,158
I wished I had kept my candle burning, the night

295
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:12,001
was drearily dark, my spirits were depressed.

296
00:23:12,689 --> 00:23:15,479
I rose and sat up in bed, listening.

297
00:23:16,470 --> 00:23:18,580
The sound was hushed, eee.

298
00:23:20,209 --> 00:23:27,501
I tried again to sleep, but my heartbeat anxiously, my inward tranquility was broken.

299
00:23:27,779 --> 00:23:31,060
The clock, far down in the hall, struck two.

300
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:36,040
Just then it seemed my chamber door was touched, as if fingers had swept the

301
00:23:38,139 --> 00:23:46,139
panels and groping away along the dark I was chilled with fear.

302
00:23:47,365 --> 00:23:52,939
All at once I remembered that it might be pilot, who, when the kitchen door chance

303
00:23:52,940 --> 00:23:57,740
to be left open, not unfrequently found his way up to the threshold of Mr.

304
00:23:57,840 --> 00:24:01,860
Rochester's chamber, I had seen him lying there myself in the mornings.

305
00:24:03,009 --> 00:24:04,740
The idea calmed me somewhat.

306
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:06,700
I lay down.

307
00:24:07,639 --> 00:24:09,360
Silence composes the nerves.

308
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:13,942
And as an unbroken hush now rained again through the

309
00:24:13,943 --> 00:24:17,259
whole house, I began to feel the return of slumber.

310
00:24:18,590 --> 00:24:21,200
But it was not faded that I should sleep that night.

311
00:24:22,189 --> 00:24:26,491
A dream had scarcely approached my ear, when it fled a

312
00:24:26,492 --> 00:24:29,700
frighted, scared by a marrow -freezing incident enough.

313
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:34,240
This was a demonic laugh, low suppressed and deep.

314
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:38,680
Uttered as it seemed at the very keyhole of my chamber door.

315
00:24:39,279 --> 00:24:43,680
The head of my bed was near the door, and I thought at first the goblin laugher

316
00:24:43,681 --> 00:24:49,599
stood at my bedside, or rather crouched by my pillow, but I rose, looked around,

317
00:24:50,319 --> 00:24:51,319
and could see nothing.

318
00:24:51,930 --> 00:24:55,788
While as I still gazed, the unnatural sound was

319
00:24:55,789 --> 00:24:58,881
reiterated, and I knew it came from behind the panels.

320
00:25:00,069 --> 00:25:02,479
My first impulse was to rise and fasten the bolt.

321
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:06,279
My next, again to cry out, who is there?

322
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:08,959
Something gurgled and moaned.

323
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:14,340
Airlong steps retreated up the gallery towards the third story staircase.

324
00:25:15,459 --> 00:25:18,400
A door had lately been made to shut in that staircase.

325
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:23,200
I heard it open and close, and all was still.

326
00:25:24,654 --> 00:25:25,659
Was that grace pool?

327
00:25:26,580 --> 00:25:28,119
And is she possessed with a devil?

328
00:25:28,639 --> 00:25:29,639
Thought I.

329
00:25:30,139 --> 00:25:32,880
Impossible now to remain longer by myself.

330
00:25:36,450 --> 00:25:38,400
I must go to my frock and a shawl.

331
00:25:39,099 --> 00:25:42,540
I withdrew the bolt and opened the door with a trembling hand.

332
00:25:43,389 --> 00:25:47,619
There was a candle burning just outside, and on the matting in the gallery.

333
00:25:48,830 --> 00:25:54,680
I was surprised at this circumstance, but still more was I amazed to perceive

334
00:25:54,681 --> 00:26:01,020
the air quite dim as if filled with smoke, and while looking to the right hand and

335
00:26:01,021 --> 00:26:04,861
left, to find once these blue wreaths issued, I

336
00:26:04,862 --> 00:26:08,520
became further aware of a strong smell of burning.

337
00:26:09,409 --> 00:26:10,479
Something creaked.

338
00:26:11,430 --> 00:26:15,930
It was a door, a jar, and that door was Mr. Rochester's,

339
00:26:15,931 --> 00:26:19,159
and the smoke rushed in a cloud from thence.

340
00:26:20,330 --> 00:26:22,060
I thought no more of Mrs. Fairfax.

341
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:25,616
I thought no more of grace pool, or the

342
00:26:25,617 --> 00:26:29,041
laugh, in an instant I was within the chamber.

343
00:26:30,020 --> 00:26:34,259
Tongues of flame darted around the bed, the curtains were on fire.

344
00:26:35,340 --> 00:26:38,987
In the midst of blaze and vapor, Mr. Rochester

345
00:26:38,988 --> 00:26:42,279
lay stretched motionless in deep sleep.

346
00:26:43,580 --> 00:26:44,580
Wake!

347
00:26:44,819 --> 00:26:45,020
Wake!

348
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:46,540
I cried.

349
00:26:46,599 --> 00:26:48,959
I shook him, but he only murmured and turned.

350
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:51,619
The smoke had stupified him.

351
00:26:52,299 --> 00:26:53,400
Not a moment could be lost.

352
00:26:54,099 --> 00:26:57,400
The very sheets were kindling, I rushed to his basin and you were.

353
00:26:58,419 --> 00:27:03,139
Fortunately, one was wide and the other deep, and both were filled with water.

354
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:08,580
I heaved them up, deluged the bed in its occupant, flew back to my own room,

355
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:14,119
brought my own water jug, baptized the couch of fresh, and by God's aid,

356
00:27:14,759 --> 00:27:18,439
succeeded in extinguishing the flames which were devouring it.

357
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:23,959
The hiss of the quenched element, the breakage of a picture which I flung

358
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:29,619
from my hand when I had emptied it, and above all, the splash of the shower

359
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:34,180
-bath I had liberally bestowed, roused Mr. Rochester at last.

360
00:27:34,939 --> 00:27:39,500
Though it was now dark, I knew he was awake, because I heard him culminating

361
00:27:39,501 --> 00:27:42,959
strange enathomers at finding himself lying in a pool of water.

362
00:27:45,110 --> 00:27:46,119
Is there a flood?

363
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:47,680
He cried.

364
00:27:48,369 --> 00:27:51,919
No, sir, I answered, but there has been a fire.

365
00:27:52,319 --> 00:27:55,400
Get up, do you are quenched now, I will fetch you a candle.

366
00:27:56,819 --> 00:28:01,700
In the name of all the elves in Christendom, is that Jane Eyre, he demanded?

367
00:28:02,470 --> 00:28:04,340
What have you done with me which sorceress?

368
00:28:05,310 --> 00:28:07,020
Who is in the room besides you?

369
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,319
Have you plotted to drown me?

370
00:28:11,169 --> 00:28:12,500
I will fetch you a candle, sir.

371
00:28:13,459 --> 00:28:15,380
And in heaven's name, get up.

372
00:28:16,139 --> 00:28:21,520
Somebody has plotted something, you cannot too soon find out who and what it is.

373
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:24,279
There, I am up now.

374
00:28:25,080 --> 00:28:27,180
But at your peril, you fetch a candle yet?

375
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:31,240
Wait two minutes till I get into some dry garments if any dry there be.

376
00:28:31,439 --> 00:28:34,240
Yes, here is my dressing gown, now run.

377
00:28:35,639 --> 00:28:36,639
I did run.

378
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:40,000
I brought the candle which still remained in the gallery.

379
00:28:41,020 --> 00:28:46,840
He took it from my hand, held it up, and surveyed the bed, all blackened and

380
00:28:46,841 --> 00:28:51,279
scorched, the sheets drenched, the carpet round, swimming in water.

381
00:28:52,319 --> 00:28:53,319
What is it?

382
00:28:53,779 --> 00:28:54,779
And who did it?

383
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:55,900
He asked.

384
00:28:57,180 --> 00:29:00,119
I briefly related to him what had transpired.

385
00:29:01,125 --> 00:29:05,400
The strange laugh I had heard in the gallery, the step ascending to the third

386
00:29:05,401 --> 00:29:10,740
story, the smoke, the smell of fire, which had conducted me to his room.

387
00:29:11,799 --> 00:29:15,996
In what state I had found matters there, and how I had

388
00:29:15,997 --> 00:29:18,900
deluged him with all the water I could lay hands on.

389
00:29:19,759 --> 00:29:21,159
He listened very gravely.

390
00:29:21,779 --> 00:29:26,400
His face, as I went on, expressed more concern than astonishment.

391
00:29:27,209 --> 00:29:29,720
He did not immediately speak when I had concluded.

392
00:29:30,950 --> 00:29:32,380
Shall I call Mrs. Fairfax?

393
00:29:32,381 --> 00:29:33,381
I asked.

394
00:29:34,180 --> 00:29:35,799
Mrs. Fairfax, no!

395
00:29:36,479 --> 00:29:37,896
What the juice would you call her for?

396
00:29:37,919 --> 00:29:38,919
What can she do?

397
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:40,380
Let her sleep unmolested.

398
00:29:41,729 --> 00:29:44,680
Then I will fetch Leah and wake John and his wife.

399
00:29:46,099 --> 00:29:47,099
Not at all.

400
00:29:47,860 --> 00:29:48,860
Just be still.

401
00:29:49,849 --> 00:29:50,900
You have a shawl on.

402
00:29:51,939 --> 00:29:55,139
If you are not warm enough, you may take my cloak yonder.

403
00:29:55,939 --> 00:29:58,599
Wrap it about you and sit down in the armchair.

404
00:29:59,159 --> 00:30:00,599
There, I will put it on.

405
00:30:01,959 --> 00:30:05,400
Now place your feet on the stool to keep them out of the wet.

406
00:30:06,599 --> 00:30:08,139
I'm going to leave you a few minutes.

407
00:30:08,700 --> 00:30:09,700
I shall take the candle.

408
00:30:10,479 --> 00:30:12,119
Remain where you are till I return.

409
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:14,119
Be as still as a mouse.

410
00:30:15,840 --> 00:30:17,900
I must pay a visit to the second story.

411
00:30:18,580 --> 00:30:19,299
Don't move.

412
00:30:19,580 --> 00:30:21,740
Remember or call anyone.

413
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:23,560
He went.

414
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:25,580
I watched the light withdraw.

415
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:31,240
He passed up the gallery very softly, unclosed the staircase door with as little

416
00:30:31,241 --> 00:30:36,020
noise as possible, shut it after him, and the last ray vanished.

417
00:30:37,110 --> 00:30:39,040
I was left in total darkness.

418
00:30:40,189 --> 00:30:42,400
I listened for some noise, but heard nothing.

419
00:30:43,189 --> 00:30:45,240
A very long time elapsed.

420
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:46,560
I grew weary.

421
00:30:47,069 --> 00:30:49,400
It was cold, in spite of the cloak.

422
00:30:50,490 --> 00:30:55,360
And then I did not see the use of staying, as I was not to rouse the house.

423
00:30:56,450 --> 00:31:01,000
I was on the point of risking Mr. Rochester's displeasure by disobeying his

424
00:31:01,001 --> 00:31:05,264
orders, when the light once more gleamed dimly on the gallery

425
00:31:05,265 --> 00:31:08,419
wall, and I heard his unshawed feet tread the matting.

426
00:31:10,020 --> 00:31:13,299
I hope it is he, thought I, and not something worse.

427
00:31:14,479 --> 00:31:17,419
He re-entered, pale, and very gloomy.

428
00:31:18,659 --> 00:31:23,099
I have found it all out, said he, setting his candle down on the washstand.

429
00:31:23,939 --> 00:31:25,060
It is as I thought.

430
00:31:26,220 --> 00:31:31,759
How, sir, he made no reply, but stood with his arms folded, looking on the ground.

431
00:31:32,810 --> 00:31:36,479
At the end of a few minutes, he inquired in rather a peculiar tone.

432
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:41,520
I forget whether you said you saw anything when you opened your chamber door.

433
00:31:43,104 --> 00:31:45,819
No, sir, only the candlestick on the ground.

434
00:31:47,180 --> 00:31:48,380
But you heard an odd laugh.

435
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:53,520
You have heard that laugh before, I should think, or something like it?

436
00:31:54,540 --> 00:31:55,540
Yes, sir.

437
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,299
There is a woman who sows here called Grace Pool.

438
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,000
She laughs in that way.

439
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:01,599
She is a singular person.

440
00:32:02,790 --> 00:32:05,860
Just so, Grace Pool, you have guessed it.

441
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:08,900
She is, as you say, singular, very.

442
00:32:09,709 --> 00:32:11,619
Well, I shall reflect on the subject.

443
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:17,396
Meantime, I am glad that you are the only person, besides myself,

444
00:32:17,397 --> 00:32:20,680
acquainted with the precise details of tonight s incident.

445
00:32:22,220 --> 00:32:23,259
You are no talking fool.

446
00:32:24,080 --> 00:32:25,080
Say nothing about it.

447
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:32,500
I will turn to your own room.

448
00:32:33,479 --> 00:32:36,639
I shall do very well on the sofa in the library for the rest of the night.

449
00:32:37,299 --> 00:32:40,580
It is near four, in two hours the servants will be up.

450
00:32:42,194 --> 00:32:45,180
Good night, then, sir, said I, departing.

451
00:32:46,659 --> 00:32:51,279
He seemed surprised, very inconsistently so, as he had just told me to go.

452
00:32:52,380 --> 00:32:53,380
What?

453
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:54,680
He exclaimed.

454
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:57,000
Are you quitting me already and in that way?

455
00:32:58,610 --> 00:32:59,759
You said I might go, sir.

456
00:33:00,889 --> 00:33:02,259
But not without taking leave.

457
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:06,060
Not without a word or two of acknowledgement and good will.

458
00:33:06,779 --> 00:33:10,500
Not in short, in that brief, dry fashion.

459
00:33:11,659 --> 00:33:16,900
Why, you have saved my life, snatched me from a horrible and excruciating death,

460
00:33:17,490 --> 00:33:22,439
and you walk past me as if we were mutual strangers, at least shake hands.

461
00:33:23,599 --> 00:33:24,900
He held out his hand.

462
00:33:25,259 --> 00:33:26,259
I gave him mine.

463
00:33:26,799 --> 00:33:30,180
He took it first in one, then in both his own.

464
00:33:31,080 --> 00:33:32,419
You have saved my life.

465
00:33:33,235 --> 00:33:35,959
I have a pleasure in owing you so immense a debt.

466
00:33:36,849 --> 00:33:37,939
I cannot say more.

467
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:41,268
Nothing else that has been would have been tolerable to

468
00:33:41,269 --> 00:33:44,040
me in the character of creditor for such an obligation.

469
00:33:45,220 --> 00:33:47,159
But you, it is different.

470
00:33:48,049 --> 00:33:50,060
I feel your benefits no burden, Jane.

471
00:33:51,220 --> 00:33:52,220
He paused.

472
00:33:52,619 --> 00:33:53,619
Gazed at me.

473
00:33:54,540 --> 00:33:59,159
Words almost visible trembled on his lips, but his voice was checked.

474
00:34:00,439 --> 00:34:01,439
Good night again, sir.

475
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:05,880
There is no debt, benefit, burden, obligation in the case.

476
00:34:07,139 --> 00:34:08,720
I knew he continued.

477
00:34:09,709 --> 00:34:12,680
You would do me good in some way at some time.

478
00:34:13,529 --> 00:34:16,459
I saw it in your eyes when I first beheld you.

479
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:19,459
Their expression and smile did not.

480
00:34:20,240 --> 00:34:21,240
Again, he stopped.

481
00:34:21,819 --> 00:34:22,819
Did not.

482
00:34:23,150 --> 00:34:24,439
He proceeded hastily.

483
00:34:25,220 --> 00:34:28,220
Strike delight to my very most heart so for nothing.

484
00:34:29,259 --> 00:34:31,159
People talk of natural sympathies.

485
00:34:31,985 --> 00:34:33,360
I have heard of good genie.

486
00:34:34,349 --> 00:34:36,500
There are grains of truth in the wildest fable.

487
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:38,700
My cherished preserver, good night.

488
00:34:39,729 --> 00:34:41,500
Strange energy was in his voice.

489
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:43,700
Strange fire in his look.

490
00:34:44,685 --> 00:34:46,779
I'm glad I happened to be awake, I said.

491
00:34:47,540 --> 00:34:48,540
And then I was going.

492
00:34:49,099 --> 00:34:49,400
What?

493
00:34:49,860 --> 00:34:50,860
You will go?

494
00:34:51,279 --> 00:34:52,279
I'm cold, sir.

495
00:34:52,720 --> 00:34:53,159
Cold?

496
00:34:53,720 --> 00:34:54,720
Yes.

497
00:34:54,840 --> 00:34:55,979
And standing in a pool.

498
00:34:56,580 --> 00:34:57,139
Go then, Jane.

499
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:57,479
Go.

500
00:34:58,180 --> 00:34:59,700
But he still retained my hand.

501
00:35:00,220 --> 00:35:01,340
And I could not free it.

502
00:35:01,700 --> 00:35:03,119
I bethought myself of an expedient.

503
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:07,099
I think I hear Mrs. Fairfax move, sir, said I.

504
00:35:08,250 --> 00:35:09,250
Well, leave me.

505
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:12,279
He relaxed his fingers, and I was gone.

506
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:15,900
I regained my couch, but never thought of sleep.

507
00:35:17,150 --> 00:35:20,377
Till morning dawn, I was tossed on a buoyant but unquiet

508
00:35:20,378 --> 00:35:23,860
sea, where billows of trouble rolled under surges of joy.

509
00:35:25,540 --> 00:35:28,298
I thought sometimes I saw beyond its wild

510
00:35:28,299 --> 00:35:32,100
waters, ashore, sweet as the hills of Bueller.

511
00:35:32,340 --> 00:35:36,316
And now and then a freshening gale, wakened by

512
00:35:36,317 --> 00:35:39,900
hope, bore my spirit triumphantly towards the born.

513
00:35:41,229 --> 00:35:43,720
But I could not reach it, even in fancy.

514
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:48,880
A counteracting breeze blew off land and continually drove me back.

515
00:35:50,069 --> 00:35:54,220
Sense would resist delirium, judgment would warn passion.

516
00:35:55,529 --> 00:35:59,000
Too feverish to rest, I rose as soon as day dawned.
